---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Lunar calendar feeds
permalink: /cal/
variants:
  - { suffix: "", label: "1st and 15th" }
  - { suffix: "-no15", label: "1st only" }
feeds:
  - id: mongol
    name: Mongol lunar calendar
    native: Монгол билгийн тоолол
    langs: [{ code: en, label: English }, { code: mn, label: Монгол }]
    festivals: Bituun, Tsagaan Sar, Ikh Düichen, Chinggis Khaan's birthday
  - id: phugpa
    name: Tibetan calendar (Phugpa)
    native: བོད་ཀྱི་ལོ་ཐོ། (ཕུག་ལུགས།)
    langs: [{ code: en, label: English }, { code: bo, label: བོད་ཡིག }]
    festivals: Losar and the four düchen
  - id: tsurphu
    name: Tibetan calendar (Tsurphu)
    native: བོད་ཀྱི་ལོ་ཐོ། (མཚུར་ལུགས།)
    langs: [{ code: en, label: English }, { code: bo, label: བོད་ཡིག }]
    festivals: Losar and the four düchen
  - id: bhutan
    name: Bhutanese calendar
    native: འབྲུག་གི་ལོ་ཐོ།
    langs: [{ code: en, label: English }, { code: dz, label: རྫོང་ཁ }]
    festivals: Losar and the four düchen
---

<h1>Lunar calendar feeds</h1>
<p class="lede narrow">Subscribe to a traditional lunar calendar in the calendar app you already use (Apple, Google, Outlook and others). Each feed adds a separate calendar layer showing the first day of every lunar month, with the full month and year, the 15th lunar day, and the main festivals. The dates are computed with <a href="https://gantemur.github.io/caltib/">caltib</a> and cover 2020–2050.</p>

<div class="stack">
  {% for cal in feeds %}
    <section class="rule-section">
      <h2>{{ cal.name }} <span class="meta">{{ cal.native }}</span></h2>
      <p class="meta">Festivals: {{ cal.festivals }}.</p>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Language</th><th>Days shown</th><th>Subscribe</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for lang in cal.langs %}
            {% for variant in variants %}
              {% set file = cal.id + "-" + lang.code + variant.suffix + ".ics" %}
              <tr>
                <td>{{ lang.label }}</td>
                <td>{{ variant.label }}</td>
                <td class="feed-links" data-feed="{{ file }}">
                  <a class="feed-apple" href="{{ file }}">Apple</a> ·
                  <a class="feed-google" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?cid=webcal://gantemur.github.io/cal/{{ file }}">Google</a> ·
                  <a href="{{ file }}">.ics file</a>
                </td>
              </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <section class="rule-section">
    <h2>Mongol auspicious days <span class="meta">Зурхайн онцлох өдрүүд</span></h2>
    <p class="meta">Балжинням and Дашням (auspicious), Модон хохимой and Тэрсүүд (days to be careful), with Tsagaan Sar, Ikh Düichen and Chinggis Khaan's birthday. Can be combined with the Mongol calendar above.</p>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Language</th><th>Subscribe</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for lang in feeds[0].langs %}
          {% set file = "mongol-auspicious-" + lang.code + ".ics" %}
          <tr>
            <td>{{ lang.label }}</td>
            <td class="feed-links" data-feed="{{ file }}">
              <a class="feed-apple" href="{{ file }}">Apple</a> ·
              <a class="feed-google" href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/render?cid=webcal://gantemur.github.io/cal/{{ file }}">Google</a> ·
              <a href="{{ file }}">.ics file</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="rule-section">
    <h2>How to subscribe</h2>
    <ul class="compact-list">
      <li><strong>iPhone, iPad, Mac:</strong> tap or click <em>Apple</em> and confirm the subscription.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Calendar:</strong> click <em>Google</em> on a computer and confirm. The calendar then also appears in the Google Calendar app on Android and iPhone (enable it under the app's settings if hidden).</li>
      <li><strong>Outlook and other apps:</strong> copy the address of the <em>.ics file</em> link and use "Subscribe from web" or "Add calendar from URL".</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="meta">Subscribed calendars refresh automatically; Google may take a day to show updates. Downloading and importing the .ics file instead gives a one-time copy that does not update.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="rule-section">
    <h2>Conventions</h2>
    <ul class="compact-list">
      <li>Lunar days are sometimes omitted or repeated. If lunar day 1 is omitted, the month's first event is on lunar day 2 and says so; if it is repeated, the second day gets a short "repeated" event.</li>
      <li>If lunar day 15 is omitted, the event is shown on lunar day 14; if it is repeated, both days are shown. Festivals on a fixed lunar day follow the same rule. Festivals fall in the regular, not the leap, month.</li>
      <li>Auspicious days follow the usual Mongolian almanac handling: a day falling on an omitted lunar day is shown on the day before; of a repeated lunar day only the second is marked; in a leap-month pair only the leap (first) month carries them.</li>
      <li>Events are all-day and marked as free time, so they do not block your schedule.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>

<script>
  for (const a of document.querySelectorAll(".feed-apple")) {
    a.href = "webcal://gantemur.github.io/cal/" + a.closest("[data-feed]").dataset.feed;
  }
</script>
